      "writtenOn": "2017-12-14T17:33:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For OMAPI compliance you need: IOError (e.g. error communicating with SIM card); SE Inserted, SE Removed.\n\nMay need to track SIM state changes (see https://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html) - UICC Reader should not allow communication until SIM_STATE_READY - I suspect that this can be handled by using an int parameter to carry the important SIM state changes. At least:\n\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#SIM_STATE_CARD_IO_ERROR\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/telephony/TelephonyManager.html#SIM_STATE_CARD_READY\n\nYou may be able to combine SIM_STATE_ABSENT, SIM_STATE_CARD_RESTRICTED, SIM_STATE_NETWORK_LOCKED, SIM_STATE_PERM_DISABLED, SIM_STATE_PIMN_REQUIRED, SIM_STATE_PUK_REQUIRED and SIM_STATE_UNKNOWN into a single \"SIM state not ready\" for OMAPI.",
      "revId": "95dccea68ed9ed9b65eb360fb177f7a8821aef91",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
